## Key Takeaways table — tying the whole week together

| Method | Cold start | Needs content | Scalable | Interpretable |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Content-based | User: ✗, Item: ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| User-User CF | Both: ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | Moderate |
| Item-Item CF | Both: ✗ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ |
| Matrix Factorization | Both: ✗ | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ |
| Hybrid | Reduced | Optional | ✓ | Moderate |

This table is worth memorizing the *shape* of, not just the cells: notice content-based is the only method that handles item cold start, CF methods are interpretable but don't scale as well (user-user especially), SVD scales and performs well but you can't explain *why* it recommended something (no clean "because you liked X" story), and hybrid is the practical compromise across all four columns — which is exactly why real systems use it.

